# Parsed CSVs and the packed payload — both regenerate from ohv1.txt by
# running the three build scripts, so there is no reason to version 56 MB
# of derived data.
#
# Note this excludes the directory's *contents*, not the directory: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded, and the Quick
# Stats cache below has to survive.
data/*
build/payload.json
build/payload.json.gz

# The Quick Stats cache is committed for the same reason ohv1.txt is: without
# it a fresh clone must pull 1.5 GB from NASS before it can build anything.
# 8 MB, already gzipped, and it is what validate_quickstats.py checks the
# parser against.
!data/qs_ohio_county.tsv.gz

# Test output
build/shots/
build/dl/

# build/counties-10m.json IS committed: it is a one-off download from
# jsDelivr, and vendoring it keeps the build working offline.

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
